


translate english day_1_9f1c2ade:


    "The wind clawed at my window all night long."


translate english day_1_75bd1c64:


    "It wandered the fields and howled like a hungry beast."


translate english day_1_b2f2e307:


    "An endless song, weaved from all sorts of voices – shrill, gentle, sneery – twined in the air."


translate english day_1_b5d94530:


    "They were shouting and laughing..."


translate english day_1_004c8f87:


    "...and arguing about something."


translate english day_1_57cbf6cb:


    "Someone was running through the snow while casting long shadows that would occasionally creep close to my bed."


translate english day_1_8038cca1:


    "Our house had a mind of its own – the creaky old mind of a building that had seen a lot in its days and was seemingly trying to share its wisdom with the inhabitants."


translate english day_1_5e399ea7:


    "The lonely house faced the forest, and the dark green thicket gazed back with its hollow eyes. Rustling, whizzing, swaying back and forth..."


translate english day_1_aa60d53a:


    "One could come out and stand at the edge of the forest to reassure themselves – there was nobody behind the crooked trees."


translate english day_1_90e30280:


    "Fuzzy silhouettes swaying in the wind couldn't possibly do any harm."


translate english day_1_16a51654:


    "It's just a play of light and shadow..."


translate english day_1_bf6e8a2c:


    "Just a play."


translate english day_1_2178dae0:


    "I knew it was just my imagination. I was already twelve, after all."


translate english day_1_c70b8af2:


    "Still..."


translate english day_1_542bfb7b:



    voice "voice/karina/10 K.ogg"
    Mam "Hey, put away your book!"


translate english day_1_1917188e:



    voice "voice/karina/01 K.ogg"
    Mam "How many times have I told you not to read at the table? It's bad for your health! Look at how slouched you are!"


translate english day_1_ecef6b19:


    "I didn't protest and put the book about Conan the Barbarian aside."


translate english day_1_049be23a:


    "I was stuck on a line I couldn't understand after reading it three times anyway."


translate english day_1_ad386629:


    "Olya had already finished her breakfast and was munching on some cookies. She was so enthusiastic she almost looked like your typical girl from commercials."


translate english day_1_f55d34d7:



    voice "voice/karina/12 K.ogg"
    Mam "You're not going anywhere until you finish all of it!"


translate english day_1_32a06ef6:


    "I, on the other hand, was still trying to drill a hole in the plate with my eyes, as if it would make the porridge disappear."


translate english day_1_1dca20e6:


    "Hazy anxiousness welled up inside. All because of the previous sleepless night, the black forest around our house and the gloomy wind..."


translate english day_1_4ff45d04:


    "The longer I waited, the colder the lumpy white substance became."


translate english day_1_13dc53a0:


    "It looked like a jellyfish from the Cousteau Odyssey. I love that show."


translate english day_1_46a6ba39:


    "I wonder how horrifying the bottom of the ocean is..."


translate english day_1_cd9a2bf3:


    "Or how cold the black forest is at night..."


translate english day_1_0e38e08b:


    "The spoon fell out of my hand."


translate english day_1_a51ad1d3:


    "Mom showered me with a cold glare from her green eyes."


translate english day_1_b7a37e34:



    voice "voice/karina/13 K.ogg"
    Mam "What did I just say?"


translate english day_1_15415c59:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/001. YA dost.ogg"
    Ant "I'll get it!"


translate english day_1_ef449e18:


    "I had ten seconds to catch my breath before battling the nasty porridge once again."


translate english day_1_bf32bfc2:


    "I felt around for the spoon."


translate english day_1_8a5d3dc7:


    "What is this, carved on the other side of the table?"


translate english day_1_91fabee7:


    "Ka-ri-na"


translate english day_1_1246aef5:


    "Ha, that's my mom's name!"


translate english day_1_49e434a0:


    "I guess she carved it out with something pointy when she was little."


translate english day_1_c77a868a:


    "She sure was a rascal, damaging the furniture like that."


translate english day_1_773ffb59:


    "She would scold me for a week if I did something similar, though."


translate english day_1_e691dcdf:


    "Should I remind her about it?"


translate english day_1_cf4072af:


    "No. She's been in a bit of bad mood lately."


translate english day_1_10648b5c:


    "I imagined her being my age, sitting under this table."


translate english day_1_1869fd53:


    "I wonder, was mom afraid of the dark back then?"


translate english day_1_37aaabdd:


    "Or the sounds coming from the attic?"


translate english day_1_2d1a12e6:


    "Or the thick forest...?"


translate english day_1_27cefc9e:


    "I imagined my grandma coming into my little mom's room, sitting at the edge of her bed, where Olya sleeps nowadays, and saying this in her soft, smooth voice:"


translate english day_1_3b3613ab:



    voice "voice/grandmother/1. Taiga.ogg"
    Gra "Taiga is a special place, little girl."


translate english day_1_5908e3e0:



    voice "voice/grandmother/2. Ona.ogg"
    Gra "It's watching you closely, sniffing you out."


translate english day_1_b31a8e34:



    voice "voice/grandmother/3. Slovno.ogg"
    Gra "Trying to discern what kind of beast you are."


translate english day_1_bb0fde72:



    voice "voice/grandmother/4.Ponrav.ogg"
    Gra "If you're a good sort - it won't abandon you in times of trouble."


translate english day_1_ee87960c:



    voice "voice/grandmother/5.A bud.ogg"
    Gra "But if you're a bad apple, it'll grab you by the side and drag you under the ground."


translate english day_1_90443588:



    voice "voice/grandmother/6.Tut.ogg"
    Gra "And that would be it."


translate english day_1_820042dd:


    "Grandma was caring, she never fought with anybody, never yelled, never swore..."


translate english day_1_e4566b49:


    "Those were the times without the maddening screams until late at night, without smashed dishes and mutual accusations."


translate english day_1_1af8038a:


    "Our parents used to love each other back then."


translate english day_1_d2786426:


    "I remember listening in on one of their conversations by chance. They were talking about grandma getting prepared for her funeral."


translate english day_1_865042d9:


    "She had already bought a casket."


translate english day_1_269223c7:


    "And she called it her 'cute funeral box'."


translate english day_1_29405cc9:


    "It waited for its time in the closet. Patiently."


translate english day_1_6dcae77f:


    "It was black, upholstered with meat-colored material on the inside. I saw it when my grandma was getting buried."


translate english day_1_a488c41a:


    "The house didn't change since the time she was alive. Only all of the photos were gone."


translate english day_1_cc0e326e:


    "Glass-covered pictures with grey faces of my ancestors. They all had a dead, but watchful look in their eyes."


translate english day_1_bd0fdb16:


    "I crawled out from under the table."


translate english day_1_4c69f865:


    "Olya was done with her cookies, and was looking at my share like a sly woodland critter."


translate english day_1_87228586:


    "I turned my gaze toward the frosted window."


translate english day_1_74977016:


    "There were a lot of dark pines outside, but they didn't grab my attention."


translate english day_1_86016b61:


    "The pattern of frost formed a picture on the glass."


translate english day_1_8d54a51e:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/002. Olja gl.ogg"
    Ant "Olya, look, it's a fox!"


translate english day_1_474007d9:



    voice "voice/olya/02 O.ogg"
    Oly "Where?"


translate english day_1_a442274d:


    "It looked almost like those optical illusion thingies they put on the back of student notebooks."


translate english day_1_198aeb72:


    "A mixture of lines at first glance, but if you blur your vision a little bit..."


translate english day_1_00fc2fba:


    "...and look under a certain angle..."


translate english day_1_5383802e:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/003. Da ne.ogg"
    Ant "Not outside! On the window!"


translate english day_1_8cce2a1a:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/004. Smotri.ogg"
    Ant "Look, here's the nose. And here's..."


translate english day_1_92ff20c6:



    voice "voice/karina/14 K.ogg"
    Mam "Hey, eat up!"


translate english day_1_0d905758:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/005. Da da.ogg"
    Ant "Yes, yes... just a moment."


translate english day_1_af0ccae6:



    voice "voice/olya/03 O.ogg"
    Oly "I don't see anything."


translate english day_1_1891cde4:



    voice "voice/karina/15 K.ogg"
    Mam "Hurry up, there's not much left!"


translate english day_1_f61b94b6:



    voice "voice/olya/04 O.ogg"
    Oly "Aaaaaah! There it is... but it still doesn't look like one."


translate english day_1_87f9a929:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/006.A ja gov.ogg"
    Ant "And I'm telling you it does."


translate english day_1_179ecb58:



    voice "voice/olya/05 O.ogg"
    Oly "Nuh-uh!"


translate english day_1_5ce7ea3e:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/007.Pohozhe_.ogg"
    Ant "It does!"


translate english day_1_4a419efc:



    voice "voice/karina/16 K.ogg"
    Mam "Stop it! These kids, I swear..."


translate english day_1_80ebae61:


    "Now I couldn't see the fox either."


translate english day_1_0eef0d0c:


    "It disappeared."


translate english day_1_790e5679:


    "Went away."


translate english day_1_31c97f8e:


    "Only the frosty patterns, similar to stretched-out nettle leaves, kept creeping up the glass."


translate english day_1_16d1eb3c:


    "My dad entered the kitchen with long, measured steps."


translate english day_1_adb88099:


    "I want to have a beard like his when I grow up!"


translate english day_1_33820e21:


    "Mom would always ask, jokingly: 'Come on, shave it off, it stings!'"


translate english day_1_47a2c0cc:


    "This was so long ago..."


translate english day_1_3cf4a827:


    "Nowadays, rumbling doors and witty comebacks were an everyday occurrence."


translate english day_1_39a76bc6:


    "Olya always covers her ears whenever she hears something like 'What's the point in all this?' through the wall."


translate english day_1_e633ef90:


    "\"It's all for your sake\", dad would reply, \"For the sake of our family!\""


translate english day_1_de00e241:


    "I always caught every sound in fear of hearing the most dreaded, the deadliest word that started with a 'd'."


translate english day_1_10acd95c:


    "D. I. V. O..."


translate english day_1_6eb7bf83:


    "I don't even want to finish it."


translate english day_1_b4ef24d7:


    "It was scary to imagine that me and my little sister could be torn apart and taken into two different families."


translate english day_1_5dded2d3:



    voice "voice/olya/06 O.ogg"
    Oly "Anyway, your fox is nothing! I have an owl on my window!"


translate english day_1_fcbb62ca:



    voice "voice/father/01 F.ogg"
    Pap "You and your owl talk again!"


translate english day_1_a7849877:



    voice "voice/olya/07 O.ogg"
    Oly "You said you believed me just yesterday!"


translate english day_1_6524aa0c:



    voice "voice/father/02 F.ogg"
    Pap "Has anybody seen my car keys?"


translate english day_1_c0028c88:



    voice "voice/father/03 F.ogg"
    Pap "I remember leaving them on the windowsill..."


translate english day_1_287dcf3f:



    voice "voice/karina/17 K.ogg"
    Mam "Right..."


translate english day_1_0eb3714b:



    voice "voice/karina/18 K.ogg"
    Mam "Maybe you did, and maybe not."


translate english day_1_809f00ce:



    voice "voice/karina/19 K.ogg"
    Mam "You're a grown man, a father of two, and still..."


translate english day_1_bf2f4834:



    voice "voice/father/04 F.ogg"
    Pap "Karina, please, stop."


translate english day_1_7ec9c1e3:



    voice "voice/father/06 F.ogg"
    Pap "Just let me get ready in peace."


translate english day_1_22967032:



    voice "voice/karina/20 K.ogg"
    Mam "Your keys are in the basket, near the phone."


translate english day_1_9770212d:



    voice "voice/father/07 F.ogg"
    Pap "Well, thank you very much."


translate english day_1_304afd1a:



    voice "voice/father/08 F.ogg"
    Pap "Anton, stop making a martyr out of yourself and finish eating already."


translate english day_1_4b23c8f4:



    voice "voice/olya/07A O.ogg"
    Oly "But the owl..."


translate english day_1_51362280:



    voice "voice/father/09 F.ogg"
    Pap "There was no owl."


translate english day_1_d2c87411:



    voice "voice/olya/08 O.ogg"
    Oly "But there was one!"


translate english day_1_e2f790bc:



    voice "voice/olya/09 O.ogg"
    Oly "It had giaaaaaant glowing eyes!"


translate english day_1_14d21c04:


    "Olya sprung up from the chair and placed her hands on her little face, imitating a pair of eyes with her fingers, the size of an apple each."


translate english day_1_6eb8c072:



    voice "voice/father/10 F.ogg"
    Pap "Last year you had {u}Babai{/u} in your closet, and now this owl?"


translate english day_1_6464d345:



    voice "voice/olya/10 O.ogg"
    Oly "B-but I saw it..."


translate english day_1_e92a1260:


    "Olya shifted her gaze back and forth from dad to mom to me, but couldn't find any support."


translate english day_1_7af699de:



    voice "voice/father/11 F.ogg"
    Pap "Have you thought about befriending it?"


translate english day_1_36cbc74b:



    voice "voice/father/12 F.ogg"
    Pap "You know, like feeding it with imaginary mice?"


translate english day_1_c8ff2149:



    voice "voice/karina/21 K.ogg"
    Mam "Don't bully our girl."


translate english day_1_b8d53edb:



    voice "voice/karina/22 K.ogg"
    Mam "She's just afraid to sleep alone because she's still little."


translate english day_1_6b146687:


    "Olya pouted her lips in rebellion and rushed into the hallway."


translate english day_1_ae748248:


    "The staircase that led to the second floor creaked."


translate english day_1_f3f50af6:


    "Mom gave dad a strict look."


translate english day_1_11726d81:


    "Oh, that look in her eyes! It's so uncomfortable to be pinned under it."


translate english day_1_4663e8a5:



    voice "voice/father/13 F.ogg"
    "Dad just snorted in reply and left, ringing with the keys he just found."


translate english day_1_80d7f865:


    "A minute had passed and the theme song from 'The Little Mermaid' echoed through the house."


translate english day_1_97870c02:


    "It was stored on incredibly worn-out cassette tape, which dad already had to glue together once."


translate english day_1_d559e945:


    "It's so easy to fix objects – by gluing them back together, for example."


translate english day_1_4011f099:


    "But how do you fix a relationship?"


translate english day_1_5587ffc5:


    "Mom moved to the living room and I was left alone, anxiously stealing glances at the window."


translate english day_1_672acd0f:


    "Olya had trouble sleeping ever since we moved to this house."


translate english day_1_85ad1048:


    "She would toss and turn or curl up into a ball under her blanket."


translate english day_1_571301fe:


    "Sometimes she would jump up in the middle of the night and turn on the VCR."


translate english day_1_8a1a06e5:


    "Cartoons helped to take her mind off all the troubles we had with the move and our parents..."


translate english day_1_7458f375:


    "And then Olya said she saw that giant flying monster outside her window."


translate english day_1_d22fee20:


    "She became obsessed with it."


translate english day_1_49aa86c2:


    "Our parents did everything in their power, they tried every little trick to get rid of those ridiculous fears."


translate english day_1_2ddd8b43:


    "Olya refused to sleep alone and didn't believe that the owl was just one of her nightmares."


translate english day_1_197c0df2:


    "After last night, I was unsure what to make of my sister's words, what to think of it myself..."


translate english day_1_6bc5d126:


    "Can nightmares be infectious?"


translate english day_1_bc5006c8:


    "That night I couldn't get a wink of sleep and ended up thinking of what to expect from my new school."


translate english day_1_6928e078:


    "There were a couple of days left before the beginning of a new term."


translate english day_1_3c09329b:


    "My imagination drew long twisting hallways that led to a classroom full of kids."


translate english day_1_81fcfa91:


    "But all the students behind their desks were simply dark figures, cut out using a template."


translate english day_1_141d2d84:


    "Circular holes gaped in the middle of their faces, and pairs of eyes blinked inside those holes. It was as if some completely different creatures were looking at me from behind the flat black silhouettes."


translate english day_1_21392046:


    "Their cruel glares, filled with icy sneers, made me shiver from head to toe."


translate english day_1_07c9f84b:


    "Will I survive here?"


translate english day_1_b90fa977:


    "Won't they gang up on me and beat me down? Stomp on me with their bloodied shoes?"


translate english day_1_68fcaad4:


    "The damn school can burn for all I care."


translate english day_1_8ecd919a:


    "I just wished for anything to happen to it, doesn't really matter what. I didn't want to go there that badly."


translate english day_1_e383dbdb:


    "I didn't want to see people who are just itching to smack me on the head, trip me up, think of a new offensive name for me, worse than the previous one."


translate english day_1_04844920:


    "I felt like the glasses I wore made me an outsider or some sort of a monster."


translate english day_1_afc290bd:


    "My gaze slid across the drawings hanging on the walls."


translate english day_1_1b62448e:


    "I couldn't consider myself a great artist, but Olya begged me to hang them. Drawing was the only thing that made me happy as of late..."


translate english day_1_9dada16d:


    "The small circle of friends I had also enjoyed my paintings. And they promised to call me from time to time..."


translate english day_1_ec326b41:


    "Sometimes I imagine mom picking up the phone and saying in a cold voice: 'You've got the wrong number'."


translate english day_1_ed139515:


    "Or: 'Anton is not around'."


translate english day_1_8644347e:


    "Anton is not around..."


translate english day_1_83e03124:


    "I imagined my future classmates lying in their beds, just like me, listening to the howls of invisible werewolves outside their windows."


translate english day_1_40b4b08e:


    "Maybe my new classmates will like me after all?"


translate english day_1_ba48469e:


    "But who would ever like a boy with thick glasses?"


translate english day_1_747ea1fd:


    "I mean, my dad used to wear glasses when he was little. And now he's married to the most beautiful woman on the planet – my mom."


translate english day_1_5bd3fb31:


    "The house creaked, pressed by the wind."


translate english day_1_141aac91:


    "The condo we used to live in – a 9-floor concrete building – buzzed with the neighbor's drill, mumbled with a TV set from behind the wall, cried like a baby from the big family next door."


translate english day_1_defcec41:


    "Our current house – though I can't really call it 'new' – was completely different."


translate english day_1_169cf186:


    "It was silent and easy-going during the day. Its shadows lay dormant in the corners, on the closet cobwebs, and under the stairs."


translate english day_1_c01038f8:


    "But they all woke up during the night."


translate english day_1_7ae5a028:


    "Something was watching me from every corner. Almost as if the old photos of my deceased family, with their ashen eyes, were hanging on the walls in place of my drawings."


translate english day_1_e0c57661:


    "The floor was squeaking, rusty drains were moaning, the attic was occupied by noisy drafts."


translate english day_1_26e041e3:


    "One could think the house was performing some sort of demonic melody."


translate english day_1_acb4f43a:


    "And then I realized I was, in fact, hearing music. It was already playing for a good while."


translate english day_1_3949419b:


    "Somewhere at the edge of my perception, I could hear a flute."


translate english day_1_762028d4:


    "It was mixed in with the sound of the wind, of the creaking old house, and my thoughts too."


translate english day_1_07780ca0:


    "I stood up and rushed to the window. I wanted to reassure myself that this music was nothing more than a product of my imagination."


translate english day_1_f7379f7e:


    "It's not like someone is playing it there, amidst the cold snowy night, right?"


translate english day_1_8d630b51:


    "Someone was dancing in the field."


translate english day_1_25410744:


    "Black silhouettes I could barely make out, with the dark forest as their backdrop."


translate english day_1_ea203a10:


    "They jumped around, basked in moonlight, bumped into piles of snow, rolled around and crawled on all fours."


translate english day_1_94c11744:


    "Stories about wolves playing under the moon came to mind. But these were clearly not wolves."


translate english day_1_ab047971:


    "They stood upright at times, circled around holding hands and whipping up snow, disappearing into the shadows for a brief moment and then coming back."


translate english day_1_0d0c618a:


    "Something bizarre was going on."


translate english day_1_6e076886:


    "Shadows dancing in the starless abyss made my imagination go wild, making me anxious at the same time..."


translate english day_1_6a467bdf:


    "Suddenly, the music had stopped."


translate english day_1_fa7e0cdc:


    "The dancing shadows froze in place and, I could swear, pierced me with their eyes."


translate english day_1_61dffb2a:


    "One of the silhouettes immediately parted from the bizarre shadow carnival and sprinted across the field with giant leaps."


translate english day_1_2797e83e:


    "It glided on squeaky snow without leaving any prints until it was devoured by the pitch-black shadow of my house which became even darker and thicker."


translate english day_1_c1a2d327:


    "My heart was jumping around like the bird inside a cage."


translate english day_1_a868d9b7:


    "I shut the curtains with a swift motion and stepped back toward the bed."


translate english day_1_7625866f:


    "They saw me!"


translate english day_1_0246c682:


    "A freezing torrent of fear washed over me."


translate english day_1_14bcd939:


    "I stood in the middle of a perfectly dark room and listened to some unwanted guest move and scrape around, looking for an entrance."


translate english day_1_4509a8ca:


    "The sound moved to the right."


translate english day_1_3310c21d:


    "Then circled around the house..."


translate english day_1_41a1b6dc:


    "Now my guest should be at the front door..."


translate english day_1_6df985dc:


    "I jumped into the bed and covered myself with the blanket as if it could protect me."


translate english day_1_ea4128e1:


    "The shackles of fear locked my muscles."


translate english day_1_24bd9c77:


    "I remembered the funeral: my grandma lying there, hands crossed on her chest, her facial features sharp like that of a tin doll..."


translate english day_1_756c5d6b:


    "Ants running up and down the legs of chairs that held my grandma's casket..."


translate english day_1_18941d23:


    "I imagined those little creatures climbing up her head and pulling up her eyelids with their tiny legs."


translate english day_1_7a007ad5:


    "Then her wrinkly eyeballs would once again move inside their sockets and she'd be able to see her grandchildren."


translate english day_1_e7aceb88:


    "I was chanting the spell she taught me throughout the whole procedure."


translate english day_1_12eab4e3:


    "And now, lying under the blanket and listening to squeaks and howls, I was repeating the same words:"


translate english day_1_c3eda6ce:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/008. Na ost.ogg"
    Ant "On the island of Buyan, underneath the blemished sun, in the sea of color blue, stands a cabin made of wood. There lay lard and ashen hair, for the spawn from devil's lair, to feast and always leave alone, God's faithful servant named Anton."


translate english day_1_6c3fdf64:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/008_1. Besy.ogg"
    Ant "Evil leave this house must."


translate english day_1_c78f2b62:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/008_2. Mertvoe.ogg"
    Ant "Ashes to ashes, dust to dust."


translate english day_1_4ce47add:


    "Bizzare sounds had disappeared."


translate english day_1_11cc5217:


    "I cautiously peeked out from under the blanket and saw curtains waving around like a hanged man."


translate english day_1_266ee386:


    "And then the night doused me with a new portion of boiling terror."


translate english day_1_2cff97ee:


    "The sound scratched at my eardrums."


translate english day_1_500a668e:


    "In reality, something or someone were scratching at the front door. Hurriedly clawing at wood, demanding to be let in."


translate english day_1_50cf24ed:


    "The door was shut."


translate english day_1_4c1ba04b:


    "Dad had become very cautious recently, so he installed a sturdy lock."


translate english day_1_dd0b9599:


    "I remember him staring at the forest intently as if he was looking for someone."


translate english day_1_22bda1bd:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/008_3. Mertvoe.ogg"
    Ant "Ashes to ashes!"


translate english day_1_5844355a:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/008_4. Zhivoe.ogg"
    Ant "Dust to dust!"


translate english day_1_6554af73:


    "I hugged my knees, placing my chin between them, and drilled the door with my eyes. It was so flimsy and weak before the might of darkness."


translate english day_1_ba2c9e1b:


    "And then..."


translate english day_1_62236cdd:


    "The doorknob twitched. Slightly."


translate english day_1_ea73f171:


    "Then it turned half-way. Once. Twice. As if the person who tried to enter had no hands."


translate english day_1_c6961b2a:


    "The doorknob tilted once more, and then..."


translate english day_1_af2f69a2:


    "Started clicking. Violently."


translate english day_1_7d47cd2b:


    "My jaw cramped from fear. My wet fingers clutched the blanket."


translate english day_1_0d26a094:


    "The door creaked and opened."


translate english day_1_4aa0ba35:


    "The wind taunted me, moaning inside the tin drains."


translate english day_1_198f008e:


    "Now..."


translate english day_1_2eec08d2:


    "Now you'll see..."


translate english day_1_cc845f1e:


    "The door was wide open."


translate english day_1_cd08da67:


    "The darkness writhed inside the carnivorous mouth of a doorway."


translate english day_1_a382b04d:



    voice "voice/olya/11A O.ogg"
    Noname "Toooo..."


translate english day_1_f0244434:



    voice "voice/olya/11B O.ogg"
    Noname "...shaaa..."


translate english day_1_fe543ef5:


    "It was as if the night itself was calling out to me, flapping its black wings and squeaking with rusty hinges."


translate english day_1_73a4d8e2:


    "I was trembling, ensnared by the web of darkness that hung in the corners of my room, waiting for the one who weaved it to come out of the gaping black hole."


translate english day_1_ea17fb6d:



    voice "voice/olya/12A O.ogg"
    Noname "Toooo..."


translate english day_1_ecc55456:



    voice "voice/olya/12B O.ogg"
    Noname "...nyyyy..."


translate english day_1_bd0134af:


    "My abdomen tightened and my chest rose up, ready to exhale a desperate scream."


translate english day_1_6f7866a6:


    "But before I was able to do anything, the darkness asked me:"


translate english day_1_fedb0a85:



    voice "voice/olya/13 O.ogg"
    Noname "Tosha, you asleep?"


translate english day_1_c8867b56:


    "My sister's pale face protruded from the thick shadows."


translate english day_1_3798af37:


    "I almost screamed from relief."


translate english day_1_fdab305d:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/011. Olja_ja_.ogg"
    Ant "Olya? I... I'm not sleeping... Did something happen?"


translate english day_1_7b90b5a9:


    "Olya frowned and stuck out her lower lip – a clear sign that she was about to cry."


translate english day_1_b049dee2:



    voice "voice/olya/14 O.ogg"
    Oly "It's there again, staring at me..."


translate english day_1_cc88885f:



    voice "voice/olya/15 O.ogg"
    Oly "Shoo her away, Tosha! Please!"


translate english day_1_6877f76f:



    voice "voice/olya/16 O.ogg"
    Oly "I'm so scared!"


translate english day_1_13b9a051:


    "The fear that was tormenting me just a minute ago crawled away and hid somewhere in my stomach. I needed to calm Olya down."


translate english day_1_fa94b44e:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/012. Eto by.ogg"
    Ant "It was just a dream, silly. Don't be scared, dreams don't bite. No one's going to harm you."


translate english day_1_76d26d0d:


    "Olya sobbed."


translate english day_1_4134a3aa:


    "She was trying her best to believe me."


translate english day_1_8114df3e:


    "But was I sure myself?"


translate english day_1_fea185d7:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/013. U menja.ogg"
    Ant "I have an idea!"


translate english day_1_2533b8e8:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/013. A poidem.ogg"
    Ant "Let's go to your room and watch the video. 'Sleeping Beauty', for example."


translate english day_1_3b5e6552:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/014. Tebe zh.ogg"
    Ant "You like that cartoon, don't you?"


translate english day_1_bd088881:



    voice "voice/olya/17 O.ogg"
    Oly "Why does the sleeping beauty have a prince and I have this scary bird?"


translate english day_1_7af48afd:


    "That question took me by surprise."


translate english day_1_d099e5ff:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/014. Ladno.ogg"
    Ant "Alright, let's watch 'Cinderella'."


translate english day_1_ee4a55c7:


    "My thoughts became tangled, fuzzy."


translate english day_1_ca0f304f:


    "What was that?"


translate english day_1_d8cac51c:


    "What studied me with its eyes while dancing feverishly under the moon?"


translate english day_1_3162da32:


    "The darkness was clinging to the window, and it couldn't be fooled by grandma's old chants."


translate english day_1_710ab669:


    "It couldn't be satisfied with a feast of lard and long ashen hair."


translate english day_1_8ff5b362:



    voice "voice/olya/18 O.ogg"
    Oly "Tosha, you coming?"


translate english day_1_05f02274:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/015. Da da.ogg"
    Ant "Yes, yes. Just a moment."


translate english day_1_a0ae02f4:


    "That's why I didn't want to laugh at Olya and her owl in the morning."


translate english day_1_84606448:


    "Who could be visiting us here, in the middle of nowhere?"


translate english day_1_318bb3b3:


    "We don't know anyone around here."


translate english day_1_410e2739:


    "So persistent."


translate english day_1_85e2dc02:


    "I felt extremely unsettled just from a silly thought that our morning guests could've come from the woods."


translate english day_1_293b775a:


    "I could barely hear voices coming from the front door."


translate english day_1_8d89e157:


    "My mind was urging me to hide."


translate english day_1_beb39457:


    "In the closet..."


translate english day_1_a13f5600:


    "Under the table..."


translate english day_1_ef348d12:


    "Behind the curtains, where Olya always hides."


translate english day_1_c9d749f9:



    voice "voice/karina/24 Tosha.ogg"
    Mam "Tosha! Come here!"


translate english day_1_c91fce2e:


    "I felt like kettlebells were tied to my feet, but still dragged them toward the hallway."


translate english day_1_de036176:


    "A couple of policemen towered over me in the doorway."


translate english day_1_b1f68214:


    "They smelled like frost and worry."


translate english day_1_91fde7d8:


    "My mom always winced and grumbled the moment she saw patrol cars: '...Worse than bandits.'"


translate english day_1_c4180775:


    "At the moment, though, she looked somewhat confused."


translate english day_1_1e497a6a:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/017. Zdravs.ogg"
    Ant "Hello."


translate english day_1_733e57bb:


    "The senior officer, who wore a grim expression, nodded."


translate english day_1_87e0de14:



    voice "voice/karina/23 K.ogg"
    Mam "A boy had gone missing yesterday. His name's Vova."


translate english day_1_fc012aae:



    voice "voice/karina/24 K.ogg"
    Mam "Look at this, please. Have you seen him?"


translate english day_1_bebdfe5f:


    "The policeman held out a photograph to me."


translate english day_1_4ee6bd1c:


    "There was a ginger boy around the age of elementary school, pictured with a wall carpet as the backdrop. He had a striped cat in his hands and wore a wide smile."


translate english day_1_3032c67b:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/018. Net.ogg"
    Ant "No, I haven't."


translate english day_1_f7d81a5b:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/01 T.ogg"
    Mil "Are you sure? Look closely."


translate english day_1_359190b6:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/019. Gde mn.ogg"
    Ant "Where would I see him? I don't know anyone around here, I barely leave the house."


translate english day_1_6440689f:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/02 T.ogg"
    Mil "Well, maybe you've seen him from the window?"


translate english day_1_43153eb1:



    voice "voice/karina/25 K.ogg"
    Mam "That's right! Your windows look straight at the forest, don't they?"


translate english day_1_17e16a96:


    "The window..."


translate english day_1_6f70514d:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/020. Net. N.ogg"
    Ant "No. I haven't seen anything."


translate english day_1_2dbc76b6:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/03 T.ogg"
    Mil "I see."


translate english day_1_2c04b420:


    "He sounded tired, but his eyes..."


translate english day_1_e107dfe7:


    "His stare, long and heavy, was full of suspicion."


translate english day_1_73d9fb46:


    "I squirmed unwittingly under the weight of guilt, which his giant shadow cast over me."


translate english day_1_04b21416:


    "The policeman finally tore his eyes from me and glanced over the hallway, the stairway and the cracks in the ceiling, which I haven't noticed before for some reason."


translate english day_1_581c1816:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/04 T.ogg"
    Mil "How do you like your new place, by the way? Getting used to it?"


translate english day_1_45a0c3e5:



    voice "voice/karina/26 K.ogg"
    Mam "Bit by bit. It's just our little daughter misses the city a lot..."


translate english day_1_b3ef5e8f:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/05 T.ogg"
    Mil "Misses the city, huh...? Have the locals been treating you well?"


translate english day_1_c6d49db5:



    voice "voice/karina/27 K.ogg"
    Mam "Yes, everything is alright, thank you."


translate english day_1_4d376e2d:


    "The policeman pierced through me one more time with his grey eyes. My head started spinning."


translate english day_1_f1fe920b:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/021.Mozhet.ogg"
    Ant "Um, can I... help you somehow?"


translate english day_1_320bee7e:


    "I asked that in a shaky voice to look like a polite boy and to end this unpleasant conversation sooner."


translate english day_1_f2e9828d:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/08 T.ogg"
    Mil "Now that I think about it..."


translate english day_1_6d8ee17a:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/09 T.ogg"
    Mil "You look just like one of my nephews, little fella."


translate english day_1_09dd643a:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/10 T.ogg"
    Mil "He's a witty boy around your age, wears the same type of goggles, haha. Always engrossed in reading those mystery novels..."


translate english day_1_5d6665c6:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/11 T.ogg"
    Mil "Told me he wants to enroll in police school when his family visited this summer."


translate english day_1_33045d65:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/12 T.ogg"
    Mil "Wanted to help other people, just like me, see?"


translate english day_1_60224ccc:


    "I felt uncomfortable. As if a distant relative, and not a police officer, stood before me."


translate english day_1_1bc011a0:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/13 T.ogg"
    Mil "You know what..."


translate english day_1_ccbfba0f:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/14 T.ogg"
    Mil "Little boys like you should stay at home, steer away from trouble. The times have changed so much..."


translate english day_1_42da6324:


    "Mom interjected in a cold voice."


translate english day_1_326666f8:



    voice "voice/karina/28 K.ogg"
    Mam "You don't say."


translate english day_1_502bd457:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/16 T.ogg"
    Mil "Ah, well then..."


translate english day_1_4e126390:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/17 T.ogg"
    Mil "What grade are you in, Anton?"


translate english day_1_b2ba102c:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/022.V shesto.ogg"
    Ant "Sixth."


translate english day_1_ee4921af:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/18 T.ogg"
    Mil "Have you made any friends here so far?"


translate english day_1_b429a198:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/023. Poka n.ogg"
    Ant "Not yet. I'll be going to school for the first time after the break."


translate english day_1_272cb7d6:



    voice "voice/tihonov/1day/20 T.ogg"
    Mil "Ah, then I'll leave you my number, just in case. Call me... if you have any new info..."


translate english day_1_40c3f83a:


    "The policemen were gone along with their shadows, the smell of cheap cologne and the photo of a smiling boy."


translate english day_1_2ce6413c:


    "His face still stood before my eyes."


translate english day_1_c41eb049:


    "I wondered what it was like for him, being all alone. There."


translate english day_1_d9b96c6f:


    "For some reason, I thought of the forest, swaying in the wind."


translate english day_1_5c9d2429:


    "What did his poor parents feel?"


translate english day_1_8c743147:


    "And what would my parents do if I'd gone missing?"


translate english day_1_fbc41078:


    "Would they cry and thrash around hysterically?"


translate english day_1_1be3917e:


    "Or would they accuse each other, like they always do, and forget about me, eventually?"


translate english day_1_40086b36:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/024. Mam a.ogg"
    Ant "Mom, this Vova... Did he go missing in our forest?"


translate english day_1_7acaef10:



    voice "voice/karina/29 K.ogg"
    Mam "Seems like it. Poor child."


translate english day_1_d0f83308:


    "I looked out the window, at the road."


translate english day_1_43b52794:


    "The police {u}UAZ{/u} drove off toward the village."


translate english day_1_75cd779e:


    "The officer's nephew came to mind when I was splitting off old paint from the windowsill."


translate english day_1_b1f7188d:


    "I remembered all the teenage mystery novels from the {u}'Black Kitty'{/u} series I've read this summer."


translate english day_1_0dbe5210:


    "Your average boys and girls investigated all sorts of mysteries there."


translate english day_1_70f4872d:


    "They looked for clues, spied on suspicious people."


translate english day_1_abf2d1a4:


    "And after a set of amazing adventures - bam! - solved any complicated case."


translate english day_1_b17f3f77:


    "They became local celebrities and must've made their parents very proud."


translate english day_1_f861ad43:


    "I noticed a trail of policemen's footprints that led to the forest."


translate english day_1_d49104d4:


    "And then it clicked in my head."


translate english day_1_5565d67c:


    "Why don't I start an investigation of my own?"


translate english day_1_cafad11f:


    "Maybe I'll find that lost boy!"


translate english day_1_7cbc52fc:


    "And I'll get a reward! Olya will be so happy!"


translate english day_1_c8aeee5a:


    "And not only Olya. Mom and Dad too..."


translate english day_1_ffa3a478:


    "Maybe they'll even forget about their quarrels for a while?"


translate english day_1_f45d6e25:


    "Maybe I'll even save us from the d-word?"


translate english day_1_bff95473:


    "I fantasized about buying Olya a Tamagotchi, and getting a cassette player and a bunch of tapes for myself..."


translate english day_1_ddc6872b:


    "And a whole box of Kinder Surprise."


translate english day_1_79f6d42d:


    "When was the last time our parents bought us any toys?"


translate english day_1_8f10d079:


    "Last autumn, I think. My dad had lost his job at the time. There's that annoying {u}song{/u} about it..."


translate english day_1_32a58535:


    "I had little to no idea what was the accountant's job like. They count money, I think?"


translate english day_1_81d449a3:


    "Neighbors used to envy us."


translate english day_1_9282395b:


    "But nowadays mom and dad barely had money to afford sweets, and dad would always divide a single chocolate bar between me and Olya."


translate english day_1_d6cdb7b3:


    "Sometimes I gave her my share, too."


translate english day_1_03b555a7:


    "No matter how much I wanted to eat sweets, she was still just a pipsqueak."


translate english day_1_ba170306:


    "I couldn't wait to go out, looking for clues."


translate english day_1_e848c4e9:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/025. Poidu.ogg"
    Ant "I'm going outside!"


translate english day_1_a4bdb71c:



    voice "voice/karina/30 K.ogg"
    Mam "Yeah, right."


translate english day_1_b94b46a2:



    voice "voice/karina/31 K.ogg"
    Mam "You want the police to go around with your photograph next?"


translate english day_1_70d41c8b:



    voice "voice/karina/32 K.ogg"
    Mam "The forest is so thick..."


translate english day_1_8f6eddb1:



    voice "voice/karina/35 K.ogg"
    Mam "What if the boy got snatched up by wild animals? Or something even worse?"


translate english day_1_8baf66f0:


    "'Even worse' – echoed through the hallway."


translate english day_1_48dec062:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/026. Da ja r.ogg"
    Ant "I won't go far. I'll stay away from the forest."


translate english day_1_aa57fbc0:



    voice "voice/karina/33 K.ogg"
    Mam "Did you hear what I said?! Or should I repeat myself?"


translate english day_1_a5e51305:



    voice "voice/karina/37 K.ogg"
    Mam "Better go pack your school bag or play with Olya."


translate english day_1_080f29fe:


    "The sound of splashing water came from the kitchen."


translate english day_1_2f71f602:


    "It meant that the argument was over and mom had the last word."


translate english bunny_hall_day1_c7fcecc2:



    voice "voice/karina/41 K.ogg"
    Mam "Anton!"


translate english bunny_hall_day1_51de0685:



    voice "voice/karina/K.ogg"
    Mam "I'll whip you if you make a single step out the door!"


translate english bunny_hall_day1_a9a61586:


    "I need to distract mom somehow, or I'll get scolded and my ass whipped with dad's leather belt."


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_3e54c396:


    "There's no time for this, mom will come back soon."


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_0c33659e:



    voice "voice/karina/05 K.ogg"
    Mam "Anton! Get your ass out of the closet immediately!!!"


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_5a95df71:


    "The dark, stuffy closet."


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_a801bc40:


    "Mom says it smells like mice, but how would she know their smell?"


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_edfaca95:


    "She hates when I stick my nose in there. She's afraid I'll cut myself on the freshly sharpened axe."


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_dadd299d:


    "And Olya can't even be lured close to it. She thinks Babai is living there."


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_d07c77dc:


    "I tried to help her fight her fears once. I opened the door and turned on a dim lamp, so she would see there was nothing but cobwebs, dad's tools and scratched walls."


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_9dfb7ff0:


    "She still didn't believe me."


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_00480f3d:


    "And I liked to hide in the closet and listen to Olya count outside: 'One-two-three, better hide from me'."


translate english bunny_pantry_day1_ed49803b:


    "And then drag her feet on the creaking floorboards, hoping that she wouldn't need to look for me in the cramped monster's den."


translate english bunny_hall_cross_3e54c396:


    "There's no time for this, mom will come back soon."


translate english bunny_hall_cross_3d275501:


    "A black cross."


translate english bunny_hall_cross_558159d2:


    "This cross had seen so many people come and go in this house."


translate english bunny_hall_cross_5121d3f5:


    "It was black as if it absorbed all human sin from the long years it was hanging under the ceiling."


translate english bunny_hall_cross_617410e6:


    "After grandma died, mom was going to take it off and hang a horseshoe in its place as a lucky charm. But she cut herself with the cross' sharp corner and almost fell from the stepladder."


translate english bunny_hall_cross_45f228b3:


    "Dad called it a sign from above and ordered the cross to be left alone in its rightful place."


translate english bunny_hall_ula_3e54c396:


    "There's no time for this, mom will come back soon."


translate english bunny_hall_ula_fdf5ca15:


    "Olya's toy."


translate english bunny_hall_ula_a6cf4ec0:


    "Mom's peg-top. A family relic."


translate english bunny_hall_ula_997717c9:


    "My mom played with it when she was little, then she gifted it to me."


translate english bunny_hall_ula_f2cc63c1:


    "Olya was next in the succession line. The toy belonged to her now."


translate english bunny_hall_ula_11c874c9:


    "She stared at the dancing spindle as if it could show her something – a fairy tale or maybe even our future."


translate english bunny_hall_ula_84d75815:


    "Now even my little sister was a bit too old for the old squeaky peg-top."


translate english bunny_hall_telephone_3e54c396:


    "There's no time for this, mom will come back soon."


translate english bunny_hall_telephone_fdf7aab3:



    voice "voice/karina/Anton otoidi ot tel.ogg"
    Mam "Anton! Get your hands off the phone."


translate english bunny_hall_telephone_8abda476:


    "My parents prohibit me from making long-distance calls, but from time to time I really want to hear my old friends."


translate english bunny_hall_telephone_8af1cf05:


    "Sometimes I would just pick up the phone, listen to the low hum of the zoomer and the distant crackling, imagining the wind howling in the ice-leaden cords."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_3e54c396:


    "There's no time for this, mom will come back soon."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_d123abbc:


    "I won't touch it ever again."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_2665ce12:


    "The decrepit and stain-covered calendar was once my favorite form of entertainment in grandma's house..."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_d67ce70c:


    "I remember waking up and running to the kitchen so I could tear off yesterday's leaf first thing in the morning. As if the coming day would get lost in the Taiga forest without my help."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_f826050a:


    "One day closer to New Years'. One day closer to grandma's funeral..."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_dc93402f:


    "I haven't touched this calendar for years now."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_6bf07a3a:


    "Since the time they started writing dark and spooky death chants that only made me gloomy instead of funny proverbs and superstitions, to be exact."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_8b59e5b8:


    "I grabbed a dusty calendar leaf with caution and it tore off effortlessly."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_06f9fbd1:


    "Sadly, the spooky descriptions from my childhood were still there:"


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_507eb4fb:


    "Seven horses carry the log, \n If seven can't carry – bring the eighth from a ferry,"


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_8f5c9c50:


    "They will take it away and never come back! \n This is the fate the log cannot escape."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_ae7aae4b:


    "I crumpled the grey leaf and threw it into the waste bin, hoping to get rid of the anxiousness that washed over me."


translate english bunny_kitchen_kalendar_77164e2e:


    "It was spreading inside me like an ink stain on blotting paper..."


translate english bunny_kitchen_radio_3e54c396:


    "There's no time for this, mom will come back soon."


translate english bunny_kitchen_radio_7a21abe7:


    "Radio" "...EMERCOM of Russia has declared the state of emergency due to adverse weather conditions."


translate english bunny_kitchen_radio_ff0ff62d:


    "Radio" "According to the weather forecast, a cyclone is moving toward the region. Expect heavy snowfall, blizzards, and snowdrifts on the road."


translate english bunny_kitchen_radio_4d890acc:


    "Radio" "Keep your eyes open and take care of yourself."


translate english bunny_kitchen_gazeta_3e54c396:


    "There's no time for this, mom will come back soon."


translate english bunny_kitchen_gazeta_0a3bf161:


    "Vertical. Nine letters. The name of the Philistine deity that protected them from viper bites and had a nickname \"The Lord of Flies\"."


translate english bunny_kitchen_gazeta_b49282c2:


    "I took a peek at mom's crossword. She would get very angry when someone gave her advice, so me and dad faked knowing the answer and being about to reveal it all the time."


translate english bunny_kitchen_gazeta_be89636b:


    "I smiled at that fleeting thought..."


translate english bunny_kitchen_gazeta_0a3bf161_1:


    "Vertical. Nine letters. The name of the Philistine deity that protected them from viper bites and had a nickname \"The Lord of Flies\"."


translate english bunny_kitchen_gazeta_e7bd502d:


    "Second letter is \"e\"."


translate english bunny_kitchen_gazeta_3fce4935:


    "Hm..."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_50429cb9:


    "The side of an old 'Ocean' freezer was checkered with my childish drawings, mom's recipes and all kinds of stickers from bubble gum with dinosaurs that Olya liked so much."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_50c84db3:


    "Among that still-life picture hung a piece of ruled paper with the phone number of the police officer who visited us."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_a2a6b537:


    "First lieutenant Tikhonov – I read inside my mind, looking at the officer's sprawling handwriting."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_626e84e1:


    "A scrap of paper was held by two pieces of a broken magnet from some old Soviet toy, and those pieces just barely covered up the numbers as if to taunt me."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_b6fce400:


    "I leaned toward it to unveil the mystery and take the piece to a safer place where it would wait for its time when I would finally find Vova and be the first to call the police with the happy news."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_7995a29d:



    voice "voice/karina/38 K.ogg"
    Mam "Anton!"


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_f9e15fbe:


    "Mom's reproachful eyes stared at me."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_249ab48e:



    voice "voice/karina/42 K.ogg"
    Mam "What do you need it for? Hands off, you'll lose it."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_4b92b006:


    "Angering my mom was the last thing I wanted, so I lowered my hand."


translate english bunny_kitchen_m_401988df:


    "Of course it won't be that easy."


translate english bunny_in_fridge1_3e54c396:


    "There's no time for this, mom will come back soon."


translate english bunny_in_fridge2_25d17cf9:


    "Meat bits for soup and a pack of pelmeni."


translate english bunny_in_fridge2_11ea4bc0:


    "Grandma kept ice cream for me and Olya there, but now I could only see meat bits for soup and clumped together {u}pelmeni{/u}. I grew to hate them already..."


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_c9bd7294:


    voice "voice/karina/A.ogg"



translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_524bb396:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/027.Mam tam.ogg"
    Ant "Mooom, something's wrong with the TV."


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_ea5d6896:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/027.Kartink.ogg"
    Ant "The picture is dim and there are stripes all over the screen."


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_9c43c7f7:


    "Mom's face became visibly distorted."


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_32441a11:



    voice "voice/karina/45 K.ogg"
    Mam "Ah, you're killing me here! So, have you had enough of shooting those stupid ducks now?"


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_5a7bf0fa:



    voice "voice/karina/46 K.ogg"
    Mam "Told you the kinescope will go dim because of your console."


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_1e2bedae:



    voice "voice/karina/47 K.ogg"
    Mam "Where will we find a TV technician in this hole, huh?"


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_423d1560:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/028. Mozhe b.ogg"
    Ant "Maybe it's just the settings?"


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_74205541:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/028. Shodi.ogg"
    Ant "Please, go see for yourself."


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_1ddcec8a:



    voice "voice/karina/48 K.ogg"
    Mam "Strange, it worked fine in the morning."


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_6a6e5ab6:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/029. Izza.ogg"
    Ant "Maybe the snowfall caused it?"


translate english bunny_talk_m_in_kitchen1_034057c2:


    "Mom rubbed her hands clean on her apron and went to Olya's room."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_fb3ac2bc:


    "I opened the front gate and went into the field."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_9e84db0d:


    "Carefully, so mom wouldn't see me from the window."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_c37ead70:


    "When I crossed half of the distance toward the forest, the snow piles became as high as my knees."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_8d8899d7:


    "I remembered my nightly fears."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_c777bf17:


    "I saw those silhouettes around here."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_0f41d736:


    "They were jumping around, holding hands."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_d543f2ac:


    "That hypnotizing music started playing in my head all on its own."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_7e5d0763:


    "In the light of day, those distant figures felt like a simple dream."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_3338894e:


    "The sun turned my nightmares to ash, but the aftertaste was still there. Distant ringing in my ears. Distorted shadows, crawling on the snow alongside me."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_ab747938:


    "And a barely audible whisper in my head. Blurry and almost kind."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_aff09a20:


    "Everything was silent."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_2218021d:


    "So silent I felt like the world was totally empty."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_7443cf16:


    "No ground, no sky, no parents, no Olya."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_cba49d3d:


    "The time reached its limit, a one-way trip that ended at the forest's piny stockade."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_6bff169a:


    "Sometimes silence was much scarier than any scream."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_3193797b:


    "Our parents would scream at each other while arguing, and both me and Olya turned to stone, listening to them."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_5668d0f8:


    "But then always came the ringing silence."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_63f2e12c:


    "Our apartment became numb a couple of days before we departed."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_70f2edfa:


    "It was hard to remember the last time mom and dad joked around, laughing, or spent time together, almost like all of it was in a previous life."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_2e94239f:


    "When they kissed with Olya present, she always frowned and snorted in a funny way."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_3012a54f:


    "But one day it all changed."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_050b0738:


    "Something important had left our home."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_818d0386:


    "And something scary filled the remaining void."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_a762bcd2:


    "It was as if a fire broke out, and our parents were hurriedly packing our belongings, trying to save themselves and us."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_8775393e:


    "From who though?"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_ccf7f737:


    "From the people with dead cold eyes, who sometimes visited us in our previous home?"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_17139a0d:


    "The eyes that only saw balls of worms on the black ground in everything."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_d3c9606e:


    "And somewhere far away a siren was going off, trying to warn us of the coming menace."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_a20cefa7:


    "..."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_84b30ed0:


    "I shuddered, сhasing away my delusions, and looked around."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_f5d4d17a:


    "There were only me, this white field and the wind that was whipping up icy dust and belts of powdered snow."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_aa3b02ac:


    "I squinted from the sun, and turned my eyes to the sunless forest."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_09785941:


    "It looked especially dark in contrast with the blinding whiteness."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_018a9dad:


    "Knobby tree roots slithered under the snow like fat snakes."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_8ee831df:


    "Rotten leaves and coniferous needles froze into the ice."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_5ee76779:


    "Dry, prickly branches intertwined, bringing up uncomfortable thoughts about fences."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_4a089bca:


    "Were they protecting the forest?"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_1eb05eba:


    "Or were they keeping something from breaking out?"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_a587d69a:


    "Some object was hanging from one of the pointy branches."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_48873ef7:


    "I tried to get closer, drowning in snow, and when I almost got to the edge of the forest, I saw a knitted mitten."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_cfec8efe:


    "It looked like a wounded bird among the hungering semidark."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_dadb525d:


    "Should I take it to the police?"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_b3d0af72:


    "Their senior officer looked gloomy, but he still reminded me of captain Casanova from my favorite TV show called {u}\"The streets of Broken Lights\"{/u}."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_21899e17:


    "He was also always anxious, with a tired look in his eyes, but still brave and strong."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_50676dab:


    "Will this mitten help them find the lost boy?"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_a9c5c32b:


    "Voooovaaaaaa!"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_73865ecb:


    "I heard a distant shout. Looked like it came from the river."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_a9c5c32b_1:


    "Voooovaaaaaa!"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_2abec546:


    "As if the trees were calling out to someone."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_b387eecc:


    "\"Vo-va!\" – resounded closer to me."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_1e0b0041:


    "Someone was standing there, behind the trees."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_9f107e88:


    "Hiding."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_68e0d9ee:


    "Vovaa!"


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_b7196517:


    "I knew someone was looking for the lost boy, but still..."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_05a7164d:


    "Something was unsettling about that figure."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_ec1c49b5:


    "Its stillness, how it was bent unnaturally toward the ground."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_810b05ad:


    "Its blackness."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_9b00f8b5:


    "There's no one there. Just branches and roots."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_b4c2fcbb:


    "It's all just my imagination."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_b42a858a:


    "A nearby bird flapped its wings loudly."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_71f88aa8:


    "A shadow split from the tree and disappeared from my sight."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_d2a856df:


    "I looked away for just a moment, but when I turned my gaze back to the same place... it was gone."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_b2acb1dd:


    "So it was my imagination, after all."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_61ab3cfb:


    "Silence reigned for a painfully long time."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_6e0a13ae:


    "My muscles were tightly sprung, my heart was beating somewhere in my throat."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_e86978c5:


    "Any noise, any little movement, any small whisper from the thicket and I'd sprint."


translate english bunny_day1_open_door_251065d8:


    "But nothing of the sort happened."


translate english main_choose2_f3f21e4d:


    "I looked at the mitten once more."


translate english run_anton_8ea934f8:


    "Lumps of snow fell from the branch and that reminded me of the sound soil makes when you throw it into the pit, on top of a casket."


translate english run_anton_838dc07f:


    "I immediately felt dizzy, as if I was balancing at a precipice."


translate english run_anton_730b1dfd:


    "I slowly backed away from my finding."


translate english run_anton_7c6b7aa5:


    "It felt like the moment I touch it a trap would spring."


translate english run_anton_416ae72a:


    "And the mouse would get caught."


translate english run_anton_fcf0fa19:


    "Someone walked on the ice close by."


translate english run_anton_2e164321:


    "My inner voice whispered:"


translate english run_anton_78e95fa8:


    Ant_m "Save yourself! Run!"


translate english run_anton_751faa30:


    "My nerves got the better of me."


translate english run_anton_f62f14b4:


    "I ran, burying my head in my shoulders."


translate english take_anton_278c9501:


    "I decided to take the lonely mitten from the branch."


translate english take_anton_f0c87a28:


    Noname "Voooovaaaaa!"


translate english take_anton_9316ba27:


    voice "voice/anton/1day/Ah.ogg"


translate english take_anton_d2890e64:


    "I stepped toward the bristly trees and tried to claim my find."


translate english take_anton_aa50f3f1:


    "It didn't budge."


translate english take_anton_6ff94951:


    "I pulled harder – the branch cracked and the mitten tore off, landing in my hand with a squishy sound."


translate english take_anton_67219d50:


    "All too heavy. Wet."


translate english take_anton_71eb9585:


    "I squeezed it without thinking and something dark spilled from it, forming a tiny string between the mitten and the snow."


translate english take_anton_64dc0ee8:


    "Steam rose from the snow pile."


translate english take_anton_deaa1dce:


    "I froze in place, studying my palms in disgust."


translate english take_anton_d7c04eec:


    "Red."


translate english take_anton_f01e3d8c:


    "The sound of cracking branches invaded the silence."


translate english take_anton_3eca4237:


    "I didn't have to think twice before running away."


translate english run_to_home_6a9684df:


    "Someone was chasing me from the darkness, breaking pine branches, closing the distance with giant leaps."


translate english run_to_home_957bc56b:


    "Snow was slowing me down. Crazy thoughts flew through my mind:"


translate english run_to_home_8c8cbb59:


    "I'll get caught."


translate english run_to_home_000f6ac7:


    "They'll get me."


translate english run_to_home_9206116c:


    "I'll get dragged into the thicket. I'll be gone. Forever."


translate english run_to_home_e9ac85eb:


    "But there was one more voice, probably one of reason. It gave me strength, spurred me on:"


translate english run_to_home_834a54ba:


    Ant_m "You can do it! Don't stop!"


translate english run_to_home_88f03c27:


    "I heard an animal roar behind me."


translate english run_to_home_a4aff293:


    "It was so loud my ears went numb."


translate english run_to_home_85c39711:


    "It felt like the sound had come from a pack of hungry beasts, rather than a single one."


translate english run_to_home_fd364890:


    "Their nostrils sucked in freezing air. They sensed my fear."


translate english run_to_home_8d3bdf3b:


    "Two giant wings flapped above my head."


translate english run_to_home_1d7a2b46:


    "An enormous shadow flew over the clearing. A hoot. A wheeze."


translate english run_to_home_d0acb615:


    "The roars were coming from all directions now."


translate english run_to_home_72ce48ac:


    "From the dried up raspberry bush. From twisted pines. From under the windfall."


translate english run_to_home_66f5b6ae:


    Ant_m "Hurry, run! Don't look back!"


translate english run_to_home_e1c5b98e:


    "It felt like I was inside a nightmare. The snowy clearing became viscous like quicksand."


translate english run_to_home_fd33c13f:


    "I was stuck in place."


translate english run_to_home_ae150216:


    "I pulled my leg from the mushy trap just to be caught in a new one, even deeper than before."


translate english run_to_home_14aa86be:


    "I continued to drown, sinking deeper and deeper with every desperate push."


translate english run_to_home_a7a2e53b:


    "Was snow ever this sticky?"


translate english run_to_home_0446cfc4:


    "I screamed in horror after realizing this wasn't snow."


translate english run_to_home_38771d7e:


    "Someone or something in the snow pile was clutching my pants."


translate english run_to_home_6016c40a:


    "I gathered all my strength and rushed forward."


translate english run_to_home_b7a9d3a0:


    "The pressure on my leg was gone, my boot slipped out of the hole and my soles were on a hard surface again."


translate english run_to_home_d1f1f6f2:


    "I reached a clear path with one jump and from there, ran to my house."


translate english run_to_home_96da428c:


    "Its' gloomy facade didn't look threatening now."


translate english run_to_home_f00bd828:


    "That house was my line of defense from the shadows that flapped their wings and the creatures that were hidden under the snow."


translate english run_to_home_a0ffc502:


    "I tripped over the doorstep and smashed into the door."


translate english run_to_home_3cf067a3:


    "In all my hurry, I still managed to notice the claw marks."


translate english run_to_home_416d78fa:


    "As if a dog was striking the wood with its paws, demanding to be let in so it could escape the cold."


translate english run_to_home_54b78c02:


    "I hadn't noticed these marks when I was leaving."


translate english run_to_home_c67c830f:


    "The heartbeat in my ears was much louder than my surroundings – I couldn't hear whether someone was following me or not."


translate english run_to_home_5c06a1f7:


    "What if... they were already in our front yard and mom had locked the door?"


translate english run_to_home_9c725bcb:


    "Drowning in fear, I pulled on the doorknob and it obediently gave way."


translate english run_to_home_6847cd7f:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/016. Otdyshk.ogg"
    "I rolled into the hallway and shut the door behind me."


translate english run_to_home_4aaa0b08:


    "Porch planks creaked as my pursuers ascended the stairs."


translate english run_to_home_ae01d647:


    "My fingers slipped off the lock and I couldn't click it into place."


translate english run_to_home_e7a1a36a:


    "I gritted my teeth and pulled hard on the iron knob, whipping it between the boards."


translate english run_to_home_f41a9fef:


    "I stared blankly at the door."


translate english run_to_home_8f36d38a:


    "Someone was standing on the other side of the pitiful, flimsy barrier that was probably less useful than blankets."


translate english run_to_home_25799acc:


    "Wheezing breath reached into the house and crashed at me in waves."


translate english run_to_home_c82b26af:


    "It smelled of pine and sweat."


translate english run_to_home_46248b4f:


    "Mom peeked out of the kitchen and chastised me with the same frigid voice she always used when talking to dad:"


translate english run_to_home_a0a9ed5d:



    voice "voice/karina/50 Chto concr.ogg"
    Mam "What exactly didn't you understand when I told you to never slam the door?"


translate english run_to_home_ba8d3236:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/030. YA slucz.ogg"
    Ant "I... I didn't mean to."


translate english run_to_home_97d7e958:


    "I snuck a glance at the door – the smell was gone, and the breath was too. If there was someone in the first place, of course."


translate english run_to_home_ff4107c3:


    "Here, mere five meters away from mom, my fear was slowly weakening, melting like snow in spring, and with it the last bit of strength I had left my body too."


translate english run_to_home_382e9cea:


    "My legs gave way. I propped myself up against the wall so I wouldn't fall over."


translate english run_to_home_70b28a12:


    "Mom's expression had changed immediately."


translate english run_to_home_403a942c:


    "The cold mask of strictness and detachment was gone. Mom looked the same as before all those quarrels."


translate english run_to_home_5d77a30c:


    "She finally saw my condition, my wet pants plastered with snow."


translate english run_to_home_cdcc65f7:



    voice "voice/karina/51 K.ogg"
    Mam "Where have you been? What did I tell you, huh?! I told you to stay home!"


translate english run_to_home_4bbb0313:



    voice "voice/karina/52 K.ogg"
    Mam "Am I nothing to you too?"


translate english run_to_home_be26a9c4:


    "I got afraid she would cry. I reached out to her like when I was very little and wanted her to cuddle me."


translate english run_to_home_860915b4:


    "But mom regained her composure fast and put on her usual face."


translate english run_to_home_22fe8a9e:


    "Her eyes shined like steel. Her voice rang out."


translate english run_to_home_b8043678:



    voice "voice/karina/53 K.ogg"
    Mam "Your dad can't find his cigarettes."


translate english run_to_home_f3770ff5:



    voice "voice/karina/54 K.ogg"
    Mam "Be honest, did you snatch them? Were you smoking in secret?"


translate english run_to_home_7fe5961c:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/031. Tam za.ogg"
    Ant "I... Th-there was someone chasing me... I... I thought..."


translate english run_to_home_12994320:


    "I stuttered as soon as I started explaining myself."


translate english run_to_home_2f37ff6c:


    "Tears welled up in my eyes."


translate english run_to_home_9cb7c145:



    voice "voice/karina/55 K.ogg"
    "Mom leaned toward me and sniffed my clothes like a beast, searching for the smell of tobacco."


translate english run_to_home_8a262830:


    "Then she squinted her eyes in suspicion and looked into the front yard."


translate english run_to_home_9c3e5fb1:



    voice "voice/karina/56 K.ogg"
    "Her expression changed in an instant and she covered her mouth with her hand."


translate english run_to_home_6f1eb768:



    voice "voice/karina/57 K.ogg"
    Mam "Look, over there! At the fence!"


translate english run_to_home_a25e6310:


    "My heart started thumping as if I became prey once again and my pursuers were following me in the field."


translate english run_to_home_2b0f5871:


    "I could swear that I've heard something scratch at the door. Just like in my nightmare."


translate english run_to_home_6dfcc245:


    "Mom beckoned me with her finger and I gathered all my remaining bravery to look into the kitchen window, facing my fear."


translate english run_to_home_3f6e98a4:


    "I could barely discern some hairy silhouettes swimming in snow through the icy winter patterns on the glass."


translate english run_to_home_75fc2f69:


    "Dogs!"


translate english run_to_home_5e76b9fe:


    "Just a small pack of strays, with no name and owner, barely reminding of the hungry monsters that live on the edge of the forest."


translate english run_to_home_4182e477:



    voice "voice/karina/59 K.ogg"
    Mam "Oh boy, were you scared of them? I think they'd rather be scared of you, Anton."


translate english run_to_home_94f672b5:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/032. Oni gn.ogg"
    Ant "They were chasing me... like a bunny."


translate english run_to_home_aed9f373:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/033. A vdru.ogg"
    Ant "And what if they're rabid?"


translate english run_to_home_b89ec521:


    "The smile had slowly disappeared from mom's face."


translate english run_to_home_116545f4:


    "Now she looked at the dogs as if it was her first time seeing them."


translate english run_to_home_d819dc66:



    voice "voice/karina/61 K.ogg"
    Mam "What if they attack Olya?"


translate english run_to_home_674dd6c1:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/034. Mam G.ogg"
    Ant "Mom?"


translate english run_to_home_85d463f7:



    voice "voice/karina/62 K.ogg"
    Mam "I wish your dad could just shoot them all..."


translate english run_to_home_bb23eca5:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/035. Mama o.ogg"
    Ant "Mom, look! They're alive!"


translate english run_to_home_ccab9095:



    voice "voice/karina/63 K.ogg"
    Mam "Huh? What?"


translate english run_to_home_cd816ec4:



    voice "voice/karina/64 K.ogg"
    Mam "Are they your friend or foe after all? Make up your mind."


translate english run_to_home_d0530b59:



    voice "voice/karina/64 Ne malenk.ogg"
    Mam "You're not a little kid anymore."


translate english run_to_home_f78f9f02:



    "Mom sighed in annoyance, and I felt so bitter that I bit my lower lip and fixed my gaze on the cobweb-ridden corner just to keep myself from crying."


translate english run_to_home_92c4dd06:


    "Welp, some detective I am."


translate english run_to_home_f3fe81cc:


    "In reality, I wasn't risking my life among monsters, but rather my pants among a pack of stupid strays."


translate english run_to_home_0907af3d:


    "And what for? What use do I have for this..."


translate english run_to_home_2a3838ef:


    "Mitten."


translate english run_to_home_5f1a5681:


    "Of course!"


translate english run_to_home_4bcba634:


    "A darkened sticky mitten that belonged to the lost boy made a squishy sound in my hand. Seems like I was clutching it the whole time."


translate english run_to_home_b3dad135:


    "That's my trump card as a detective!"


translate english run_to_home_dc140370:


    "I hurried to present this clue to my mom."


translate english run_to_home_7f2a3844:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/032. Mam sm.ogg"
    Ant "Mom, look, this is Vova's mitten!"


translate english run_to_home_fd7be0bc:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/032. Nu tog.ogg"
    Ant "That boy the police were asking about in the morning!"


translate english run_to_home_91ca1acd:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/032. Ona vs.ogg"
    Ant "It's drenched in blood! I found it hanging on a tree! I can show where!"


translate english run_to_home_86de52c0:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/032. Davai.ogg"
    Ant "Let's call the police right away! Like the officer had told us to..."


translate english run_to_home_c94e28a8:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/032. Mam gl.ogg"
    Ant "Mom, look!"


translate english run_to_home_bff8fd57:



    voice "voice/karina/66 K.ogg"
    Mam "Ew!"


translate english run_to_home_633611dc:


    "A shadow of doubt slowly crept onto mom's contorted face."


translate english run_to_home_a8cae514:


    "As if she was trying to remember something distant. Like someone tries to remember their dream, but the images slip away."


translate english run_to_home_eb09aba8:



    voice "voice/karina/67 K.ogg"
    Mam "Stop it this moment!"


translate english run_to_home_305dd4d2:



    voice "voice/karina/68 K.ogg"
    Mam "Olya will go insane if she hears you!"


translate english run_to_home_ae95987c:



    voice "voice/karina/69 K.ogg"
    Mam "She already has trouble sleeping and whines all the time."


translate english run_to_home_696b0f31:



    voice "voice/karina/70 K.ogg"
    Mam "And you joke around like this!"


translate english run_to_home_92fbe260:


    "At that moment I realized the mitten was actually wet from snow."


translate english run_to_home_64014dd6:


    "There was no blood whatsoever."


translate english run_to_home_1d1ed326:


    "I wanted to sink through the floor from embarrassment."


translate english run_to_home_332e841c:



    voice "voice/karina/71 K.ogg"
    Mam "Come here, my boy who cried wolf..."


translate english run_to_home_3465e4d7:



    voice "voice/karina/72 K.ogg"
    Mam "Oh, don't just stand there, come take your pills!"


translate english run_to_home_ec1fca1a:


    "A golden-colored pill, reminiscent of a dead wasp, fell onto my palm."


translate english run_to_home_259c0f7d:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/033. YA uzhe.ogg"
    Ant "I already took one during breakfast..."


translate english run_to_home_7f2e261e:



    voice "voice/karina/73 K.ogg"
    Mam "Don't talk over me."


translate english run_to_home_a95c09ac:



    voice "voice/karina/74 K.ogg"
    Mam "I told you to stay home, and you..."


translate english run_to_home_550c764b:



    voice "voice/karina/75 K.ogg"
    Mam "Dad would've given you a good whipping for that!"


translate english run_to_home_91f3dc41:



    voice "voice/karina/76 K.ogg"
    Mam "Come on, take it, or you won't be able to sleep at night. And you have school tomorrow."


translate english run_to_home_709e0c31:


    "So I had to swallow the bitter medication, drinking it down with similarly awful water that gave off a taste of chlorine."


translate english run_to_home_02d8e55a:


    "Maybe it wasn't Vova's mitten."


translate english run_to_home_840db1a8:


    "Maybe it wasn't a mitten at all."


translate english run_to_home_50a68eb9:


    "Just like the forest monsters."


translate english run_to_home_a073be25:


    "And Olya's owl..."


translate english run_to_home_a832fa6d:


    "Am I going mad?"


translate english run_to_home_19d193f4:


    "What's happening to me?"


translate english run_to_home_e38e8428:


    "Either the pill had an immediate effect, or my overexerted brain didn't let fear inside anymore."


translate english run_to_home_43c85036:


    "Serenity washed over me, bringing yawny indifference along with it."


translate english run_to_home_9f259c87:



    voice "voice/karina/77 K.ogg"
    Mam "Anton! You done? See, you can do it when you try."


translate english run_to_home_d45b220b:



    voice "voice/karina/78 K.ogg"
    Mam "Take off your coat! Are you asleep?"


translate english run_to_home_ef9e8302:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/034. Net ma.ogg"
    Ant "No, mom, I was just thinking..."


translate english run_to_home_6c10224f:



    voice "voice/karina/79 K.ogg"
    Mam "What about, I wonder?"


translate english run_to_home_cb3e1037:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/035. Tak gl.ogg"
    Ant "It's... just something silly."


translate english run_to_home_f8485be8:


    "Mom scrutinized me with suspicious eyes."


translate english run_to_home_5d79966b:


    "As if she wasn't sure she was looking at her own son and not some doppelganger that came from the forest."


translate english run_to_home_a8b046cf:



    voice "voice/karina/80 K.ogg"
    Mam "Is everything alright?"


translate english run_to_home_51293679:



    voice "voice/karina/81 K.ogg"
    Mam "You had the exact same expression when the policeman asked you about the window..."


translate english run_to_home_779c8aa6:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/036. Vse no.ogg"
    Ant "I'm alright, mom."


translate english run_to_home_da8807ab:



    voice "voice/karina/83 K.ogg"
    "She heaved a deep sigh."


translate english run_to_home_9f98221b:



    voice "voice/karina/82 K.ogg"
    Mam "Fine."


translate english run_to_home_ce2a8eb5:


    "It seemed like the house had changed."


translate english run_to_home_29794a11:


    "The sofa's fabric had become discolored."


translate english run_to_home_2f2f64ab:


    "Fingerprints appeared on the bathroom tiles."


translate english run_to_home_3963ee02:


    "The lightbulbs also felt different – dimmer and yellower."


translate english run_to_home_88b7bce2:


    "Even the saliva inside my mouth had a different taste."


translate english run_to_home_ae38163b:


    "A melody from 'Alladin' could be heard from the upper floor – Olya was done rewatching her favorite 'Little Mermaid' episodes and switched to other tapes."


translate english run_to_home_a924fbf9:


    "I slowly changed into my home clothes, stopped before the sink and studied my reflection in the mirror, like I was trying to solve one of those 'spot the difference' puzzles."


translate english run_to_home_5cf98128:


    "Then I went upstairs."


translate english run_to_home_f52f8964:


    "Jaffar's and Iago's voices died down."


translate english run_to_home_49fdae1e:


    "I walked past Olya's bedroom and slipped into my own."


translate english bunny_anton_room_circle_a02ae117:


    "The forest didn't look as grim during the day."


translate english bunny_anton_room_circle_367f4057:


    "Entangled tree branches in the distance and the snowy field between our house and the forest brought sleepiness to my eyes."


translate english bunny_anton_room_circle_af804bf2:


    "But sometimes I would still catch myself looking in the window at the icy treetops instead of doing my homework."


translate english bunny_anton_room_circle_132152f9:


    "How strange, I remember moving this curtain..."


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_9a1123e2:


    "My triceratops figurine."


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_3620d362:


    "I know about all sorts of dinosaurs: velociraptors, afrovenators, hypsilophodonts..."


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_376a62b5:


    "I remember going to the movies to see 'Jurassic Park' back when we still lived in the city and taking pictures with the T-rex in the hall."


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_335f07b2:


    "It turned its head and roared."


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_853c61cb:


    "It was awesome."


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_78002136:


    "And next to it was a Robotech transformer."


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_b6142eab:


    "I love this cartoon!"


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_3925ec3d:


    "When a jet fighter speeds up in the intro among the sounds of blaster fire, you know your next twenty minutes will surely be amazing."


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_bdf18d00:


    "Zentraedi space station is captured! Rick, get ready for battle!"


translate english bunny_anton_room_toys_292b87ff:


    "My toys – a triceratops and a Robotech."


translate english bunny_anton_room_picture_5851df70:


    "I've dreamt of becoming an artist since dad bought me my first comic book."


translate english bunny_anton_room_picture_23593fec:


    "{u}\"Fly\"{/u} magazine was the coolest. I especially liked the big space-related edition with alien monsters and that funny episode about a gendarme."


translate english bunny_anton_room_picture_0769dad2:


    "I started drawing all kinds of stuff since that day, and I seem to be getting pretty good at it."


translate english bunny_anton_room_picture_95c3f0db:


    "One of my letters even got published in 'Fly' once. Maybe someday they'll even publish my comic?"


translate english bunny_anton_room_picture_bff4b7ac:


    "My best works."


translate english bunny_anton_room_book_7141b782:


    "'Monsters, ghosts, UFOs.'"


translate english bunny_anton_room_book_80638b6e:


    "The Encyclopedia of Paranormal Phenomenon from Rosman Publishing. I've learned about the Loch-ness monster, Medusa Gorgon and Big Foot from there."


translate english bunny_anton_room_book_c2f42282:


    "Olya is always scared of the book."


translate english bunny_anton_room_book_db8db4d4:


    "She could barely handle sifting through the monster and alien sections with me, but the middle part where they start to talk about ghosts really freaked her out."


translate english bunny_anton_room_book_f2f930ff:


    "I even remember hunting ghosts after I'd read that book: I measured the distance between items on my table every evening and checked if they moved due to some supernatural force come the morning."


translate english bunny_anton_room_book_08614dfc:


    "They didn't."


translate english bunny_anton_room_book_54e73c3f:


    "But to be honest, what was I expecting? To meet Casper the Ghost?"


translate english bunny_anton_room_book_23d2cfc2:


    "I know this book by heart already."


translate english anton_room_continue1_c19cd09b:


    "One of the drawers was empty. I hid the policeman's phone number there."


translate english anton_room_continue1_411a21e5:


    "This simple action drained the last bit of strength from me."


translate english anton_room_continue1_75c98029:


    "I sat on the bed."


translate english anton_room_continue1_a6fa8f66:


    "And only then I noticed: there was someone behind the curtains."


translate english anton_room_continue1_1c6f6db7:


    "My tired hand dropped to the sheets."


translate english anton_room_continue1_08744949:


    "Whether it was due to medication I took or the stress I underwent, the room began to contort, as if the wind was blowing the walls out like a pair of sails."


translate english anton_room_continue1_db2e3efd:


    "The corners of the room bent and undulated."


translate english anton_room_continue1_b18f6c7a:


    "The only stable thing in the whole room was the figure between the windowsill and the curtains. A flimsy piece of cloth was stuck to my hidden visitor."


translate english anton_room_continue1_8b62d6d5:


    "Just like a shroud."


translate english anton_room_continue1_e73f1a54:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/037. Olja.ogg"
    Ant "Olya?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_b3b008b8:


    "Who else would be standing there?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_e58de41c:


    "I stood up and licked my dried up lips."


translate english anton_room_continue1_3117f566:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/038. Olja ocz.ogg"
    Ant "Yeah, Olya, it's so funny."


translate english anton_room_continue1_f1d0873a:


    "The silhouette was unmoving."


translate english anton_room_continue1_16e27c38:


    "It was enveloped softly by the curtains. As if there was a thick layer of darkness there, not a human being."


translate english anton_room_continue1_53b97452:


    "I reached toward the curtains."


translate english anton_room_continue1_66cd0b98:


    "Badum, badum, beat my heart, controlled by medication."


translate english anton_room_continue1_aa427784:


    "The wind sang in the field with a chorus of voices."


translate english anton_room_continue1_7c0f183b:


    "For a second, I wanted to return to the bed, just lie down and watch the person behind the curtain, knowing full well they were looking back at me."


translate english anton_room_continue1_e5926482:


    "They're looking without blinking, waiting for me to fall asleep."


translate english anton_room_continue1_e28d37f4:



    voice "voice/olya/19 O.ogg"
    Oly "Gotcha!"


translate english anton_room_continue1_a990ceab:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/039. Da ja s.ogg"
    Ant "I knew it was you from the beginning."


translate english anton_room_continue1_b20ddb77:


    "A blindingly bright halo lit up above Olya's head with the setting sun as the background."


translate english anton_room_continue1_50eab00b:


    "My sister was shining."


translate english anton_room_continue1_7dc76bc3:


    "When she was just a baby, dad always used to say she was shining with happiness."


translate english anton_room_continue1_9da7c877:


    "I always retorted:'But dad, she's not some flashlight!'"


translate english anton_room_continue1_274ecd64:


    "But I brought her to the window one day and sunlight poured on her smiling face."


translate english anton_room_continue1_cc77dfb8:


    "I felt like I was holding a light-woven child."


translate english anton_room_continue1_945b0b8e:



    voice "voice/olya/20 O.ogg"
    Oly "Why did the police come? Did you do something?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_c8834e16:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/040. Net ko.ogg"
    Ant "No, of course not."


translate english anton_room_continue1_d20d8e1d:



    voice "voice/olya/21 O.ogg"
    Oly "It's because of the owl, isn't it?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_dde5ccfc:


    "I showed her a worried smile and rubbed her head."


translate english anton_room_continue1_37fd464b:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/041. Odin m.ogg"
    Ant "A boy got lost in the woods."


translate english anton_room_continue1_5c9b9860:



    voice "voice/olya/22 O.ogg"
    Oly "Oh... he must be really cold out there."


translate english anton_room_continue1_46df5e6f:



    voice "voice/olya/23 O.ogg"
    Oly "Will they find him?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_91c104f7:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/042. Objazat.ogg"
    Ant "They will."


translate english anton_room_continue1_5d946dbf:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/042.Uczastko.ogg"
    Ant "The police are going house to house, showing his photo to everybody."


translate english anton_room_continue1_e67a3621:


    "Olya traversed the room with care and pressed her tiny palms against the window."


translate english anton_room_continue1_01dc159c:



    voice "voice/olya/24 O.ogg"
    Oly "And why are they going to the houses, and not the forest?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_79bad9bb:



    voice "voice/olya/38 O.ogg"
    Oly "Are they scared?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_3bd0e75a:


    "The question caught me off guard."


translate english anton_room_continue1_1761c2e4:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/043. Milici.ogg"
    Ant "The police aren't scared of anything."


translate english anton_room_continue1_e256ad18:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/043. I les.ogg"
    Ant "They've already scouted the forest..."


translate english anton_room_continue1_3c1aed29:


    "I changed the topic."


translate english anton_room_continue1_aa6a3d99:


    "As if trying to get Olya as far away as possible from the forest thicket."


translate english anton_room_continue1_a7ab0e5b:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/044. Esli ja.ogg"
    Ant "We may get a reward if I go and find this boy by myself."


translate english anton_room_continue1_0d7bd550:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/044. Kuczu v.ogg"
    Ant "A lot of stuff, like in the 'Wheel of Fortune'."


translate english anton_room_continue1_8987564e:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/044. Klevo.ogg"
    Ant "Sounds cool, right?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_2ed51c80:


    "Olya wasn't listening to me."


translate english anton_room_continue1_2a0948a0:


    "She asked in a hushed voice, while piercing the forest with incredibly adult eyes, uncharacteristic for her:"


translate english anton_room_continue1_9a2edb83:



    voice "voice/olya/26 O.ogg"
    Oly "What if the owl got him...?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_2622af20:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/045. Erunda.ogg"
    Ant "Nonsense!"


translate english anton_room_continue1_c223c2ec:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/045. Ne mozh.ogg"
    Ant "An owl won't be able to lift a human."


translate english anton_room_continue1_3d61b29c:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/045. No vot.ogg"
    Ant "But you know what..."


translate english anton_room_continue1_ff6ca4d3:


    "I was picking my words with utmost care."


translate english anton_room_continue1_bf56e019:


    "I forced them out of my overexerted brain."


translate english anton_room_continue1_a5b5ba35:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/046.Ty v le.ogg"
    Ant "Stay away from the forest. I think it's..."


translate english anton_room_continue1_939392ab:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/046.Kak by.ogg"
    Ant "How should I put it... It's cursed or something."


translate english anton_room_continue1_7f782eac:



    voice "voice/olya/27 O.ogg"
    Oly "Just like in a fairy tale?"


translate english anton_room_continue1_883b488f:



    voice "voice/anton/1day/047. Net. S.ogg"
    Ant "No. More like in that spooky tape our parents hide from us."


translate english anton_room_continue1_88cbc050:


    "Olya shivered and stole a glance at the window."


translate english anton_room_continue1_d6e620e7:


    "As I looked at my sister, my heart was tearing apart."


translate english anton_room_continue1_24dc5172:


    "She was so fragile! It was so easy to stifle her light!"


translate english anton_room_continue1_5503f338:


    "A gust of wind – and her small fire would be gone."


translate english anton_room_continue1_d4b2a3e5:


